Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: support TB320FC HI1339, S5K4H7 and SC202CS

Add fixed full-resolution RAW10 modes using the device's 24 MHz tables.
Register sequences and delays were decoded from TB320FC vendor sensor
modules; source SHA256 values are embedded alongside each table. No
proprietary HAL executable or tuning blob is included.

Register semantics cross-checked against these GPL sensor drivers:
- Samsung HI1339 (Samsung Electronics, 2022):
  https://github.com/VH-Devices/android_kernel_samsung_a24/tree/9ca068ff2a485c85841d8b1fa5da529d200df44b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/common/v1_1/hi1339_mipi_raw
- SC202CS exposure/gain (guf296 <guf296@126.com>, 2026):
  https://github.com/GUF296/linux/blob/2f50ae59b2db01e7018889c907fcf64c6a135e2b/drivers/media/i2c/y700-smartsens.c

Local implementation uses V4L2 CCI, runtime PM and standard exposure/gain
controls. HI1339 line timing is normalized to pixel units; LINK_FREQ is
independent from pixel-array timing. Only the full-resolution modes are
exposed. Autofocus, flash and ISP tuning are outside this initial driver.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
index 5c52007f9..2516e83a3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -1814,3 +1814,12 @@ config VIDEO_MAX96717
 endmenu
 
 endif # VIDEO_DEV
+
+config VIDEO_ASPHALT_SENSORS
+ tristate "Lenovo TB320FC RAW10 sensors"
+ depends on I2C && VIDEO_DEV
+ select V4L2_CCI_I2C
+ select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
+ select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
+ help
+   HI1339 rear, S5K4H7 front and SC202CS macro camera capture.
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
index d04bd5724..bbb28046c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
@@ -174,3 +174,5 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_VPX3220) += vpx3220.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_WM8739) += wm8739.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_WM8775) += wm8775.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_INTEL_CVS) += cvs/
+
+obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_ASPHALT_SENSORS) += asphalt-sensors.o
